airunner for Debian
------------------

This is the SERVICES-ONLY apt packaging of AIRunner (issue #2237). It
contains no Qt desktop client. The package targets Ubuntu 26.04 amd64;
the candidate must pass a clean install and daemon health check before
apt promotion. What it contains:

  * Architecture-specific frozen CORE runtime built with the pinned
    PyInstaller profile. Its console command aliases in /usr/bin preserve
    SERVICE_CONSOLE_SCRIPTS dispatch.
  * systemd unit airunner-headless.service, enabled on install,
    running loopback-only by default (daemon 127.0.0.1:8188,
    HTTP 127.0.0.1:8080).
  * Default config seeded to /etc/airunner/daemon.yaml on first
    install; writable state in /var/lib/airunner, logs journaled
    (file logging only when the daemon config enables it).

airunner-common 6.1.8 source is byte-verified in
debian/vendor/README.source and is included in the frozen runtime. Python
dependencies are resolved from package/constraints-linux-core.txt rather
than Ubuntu's Python package catalog.

ML runtimes, model weights, and GPU libraries are not included in this
package. The daemon reports missing-runtime diagnostics when an optional
runtime is unavailable. Separately provisioned ML runtimes remain outside
this package.

Config: edit /etc/airunner/daemon.yaml, then
`systemctl restart airunner-headless`. Logs: `journalctl -u
airunner-headless`.

Port matrix (loopback-only by default)
-------------------------------------
  * Daemon control plane: 127.0.0.1:8188, from
    /etc/airunner/daemon.yaml (seeded from
    debian/daemon.yaml, mirroring DaemonConfig defaults).
  * HTTP API: 127.0.0.1:8080, from AIRUNNER_HTTP_PORT in the
    systemd unit. `curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/health` is the
    operator health check.
The two ports are different surfaces: the daemon port speaks the
internal control plane, the HTTP port serves the FastAPI API.

Environment precedence
----------------------
The shipped unit pins AIRUNNER_HTTP_PORT=8080 and
AIRUNNER_LLM_ON=1. Do not edit the shipped unit: override with
`systemctl edit airunner-headless` (an Environment= drop-in),
then `systemctl restart airunner-headless`. The daemon port has
no unit override: it comes from /etc/airunner/daemon.yaml alone.

